# HakiOS fragment: the Google Tensor G5 ("laguna", lga) -- what is true of the SoC, whatever Pixel 10 it is in (frankel, blazer,
# mustang). Eight cores, each in an affinity field of its own (MPIDR Aff1 = 0-7): two Cortex-A520s, five Cortex-A725s, a Cortex-X4,
# all ARMv9.2, so what the boot core says it can do every core can. The interrupt controller is a GICv3 whose redistributors are
# GICv4 frames of 256 KB (osfmk/arm64/gic_v3_irq.c walks them by GICR_TYPER.VLPIS); the loader's platform_frankel says where.
# None of the common repository's SoC drivers is this SoC's: they are Qualcomm's (EPSS, the SPMI PMIC, the TSENS sensors).
CONFIG_SOC="lga"
# The first boot: the kernel alone on core 0, where the boot loader left the phone (README.md, "Bring-up"). More cores
# (bootcpu=7 cpus=8) need the boot shim's PSCI to start them at EL1, which QEMU has seen and the phone has not.
# CONFIG_CPUS is not set
# CONFIG_BOOTCPU is not set
# CONFIG_CPUFREQ is not set
# CONFIG_SOCINFO is not set
# CONFIG_THERMAL is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_CPUFREQ is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOCINFO is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_THERMAL is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_PMIC is not set
